+# RHT v0.1 — robustness and readout budgets
+
+With m=min(a,N*epsilon)/2, J=max(a,25*N), choose eta<=3*m/(62*N), B_eta=m*eta^2/2 and delta_eta=eta*sqrt(m/(2*J)). A static gauge/species-phase invariant Hamiltonian error with gradient <=nu_star=m*eta/16 preserves all-time trapping about the nominal balanced orbit from that initial ball. On zero Gauss a compact invariant minimizing set exists within eta/8, stable as a set. This is not persistence of a unique unchanged stationary orbit.
+
+For time-dependent errors require both the same uniform gradient cap and integral_0^T ||grad partial_t V_t||_tube dt<=nu_star. The proof keeps total nominal energy below 7*B_eta/8 through T. An exact resonant oscillator demonstrates that instantaneous smallness alone cannot yield a generic all-time guarantee. A separate forcing-only work/displacement contract is provided.
+
+Coefficient sufficient condition: A*eta+N*((1+12*eta)*K+14*G+3*D)<=m*eta/16. The errors are typed as kinetic, normalized diamond, relative incidence hopping and scalar site detuning. Uniform detuning is a free constant on the norm surface.
+
+Each complex loop error is <21*eta. Real classification survives with eta<=min(R0,epsilon/1680) and instrument error per channel<=epsilon/80. Oriented phase instrument L2 error<=(5/2)*sqrt(epsilon) fits the prior 26-label budget. All use the declared Frobenius/unit-matter-sphere metric and normalized readout, not laboratory units.
+
+Thirty exact/symbolic checks, six floating synthetic gradient/readout fixtures, and eight PDF pages visually checked. No new interval cells; inherited NEB certificate remains conditional support. Development, no registry entry. Independent review pending; physical promotion 0.
