k through an exact ratio identity. Degree-weighted glued carriers fail a separate commensurability test. The adjoint/mass metric conventions and all exclusions remain explicit; native selection is open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/metric-admission/">Inspect source metric admission →</a></article><article class="claim" id="native-admission-v01"><div class="eyebrow">14 October 2026 · Reading edition 0.9</div><h2>Native spectral admission has explicit residual floors</h2><p>The default clock has exact common-rate residual minima3,7√15−25 and2 across the three declared unit-metric classes. Arbitrary identical copies cannot create exact full-generator agreement. A retained endpoint-alias witness has zero endpoint error despite a nonzero generator residual, keeping the error-budget inference scoped.</p><a class="text-link" href="/native-admission/">Inspect native residuals and aliases →</a></article><article class="claim" id="programmed-clock-v01"><div class="eyebrow">14 October 2026 · Reading edition 0.8</div><h2>A supplied clock, an engineered Hodge path, and two scoped limits</h2><p>The finite carrier has a constant history Hamiltonian. Rational path metrics and identity padding give an ordinary graph-Hodge representation, with clock and complete return accounted. Odd full-carrier equivalence and unit-metric single-tetrahedron full embedding have explicit obstructions. Native operator/source admission and protected export remain open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/programmed-clock/">Inspect the coherent clock and admission gate →</a></article><article class="claim" id="joint-carrier-v01"><div class="eyebrow">14 October 2026 · Reading edition 0.7</div><h2>A finite-window joint carrier with complete accounting</h2><p>A supplied reversible gate retains each old state and receipt. A finite master clock schedules B payload resets using B prepared donors; all consumed blocks become outgoing records. The construction proves a declared window, shows dirty-reuse failure after wrap, and keeps native coupling, physical resources and complete restart open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/joint-carrier/">Inspect clock, memory and reset supply →</a></article><article class="claim" id="hodge-rsp-v01"><div class="eyebrow">14 October 2026 · Reading edition 0.6</div><h2>The strict Hodge realization class has an explicit obstruction</h2><p>An exact total finite-image factor of reversible Hodge evolution can decode only RSP fixed states. Prepared trace encoding remains possible before wrap. The audit separates finite-image, finite-order, stable-recurrence and conserved-stock assumptions; broader native realization and human review remain open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/realization/">Inspect the realization contracts →</a></article><article class="claim" id="rsp1-v01"><div class="eyebrow">14 October 2026 · Reading edition 0.5</div><h2>A complete finite candidate, with its stopping debts visible</h2><p>RSP-1 drives two source-bound close/hold response choices from prepared stock and finite bank registers. Exact conditional termination, close pulse balance and hold latching are recorded. Parallel constructor checks and a separate AI scope audit passed; native realization and independent human review remain open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/source-programme/">Compare the paired programmes →</a></article><article class="claim" id="response-contract-v01"><div class="eyebrow">14 October 2026 · Reading edition 0.4</div><h2>The missing response law is now a typed source contract</h2><p>The finite response fiber has 2^i masks on i intact-null addresses. Count receipts and address receipts have different information requirements. A structural validator and synthetic specimen make the source gate reviewable. The prior presentation review is acknowledged; this new development result awaits independent adversarial review.</p><a class="text-link" href="/source-contract/">Explore the contract →</a></article><article class="claim" id="dependency-update-v03"><div class="eyebrow">14 October 2026 · Reading edition 0.3</div><h2>Polarity and action dependencies</h2><p>Source-bound premises, constitutive choices and evaluation gates now have an explicit scoped graph. Eight change scenarios identify affected uses while retaining conditional mathematics. Absolute clock and native event-source gates remain open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/dependencies/">Explore the dependencies →</a></article><article class="update-card"><span class="eyebrow">15 October 2026 UTC · theorem milestone v0.1</span><h2>A typed gauge-transport construction and its curvature boundary</h2><p>The dedicated theorem manuscript proves local frame covariance, signed tetrahedral relabeling covariance and conserved support for unitary Hasse-link transport. On the filled tetrahedron, a nilpotent transport boundary is pure gauge. Curved transport remains admissible with an explicit correction to the Hodge-square identity.</p><p>A single incidence phase of π/2 gives the exact positive frequency set √2, 2, √6 with multiplicities 1, 5, 1. The result supplies a candidate finite analogue test; it does not derive Standard Model couplings. Independent review and physical correspondence remain pending; physical promotion 0.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/papers/#gauge-transport-v01">Read theorem and replay →</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/sources/gauge-transport-v0.1/GAUGE_BRIDGE_CONTRACT_v0.1.json">Bridge contract ↓</a></p></article><article class="update-card"><span class="eyebrow">15 October 2026 UTC · source intake v0.1</span><h2>Additional-workstream narrative manuscript captured</h2><p>Review candidate 0.15 is preserved as a separate synthesis with its original PDF hash, complete text extract and page index. Intake preserves source status and leaves scientific replay, independent review and physical correspondence gates unchanged.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/papers/#narrative-v015">Read the manuscript →</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/sources/